    {
      "id": "vlR0T8YLrc5G8XFWoBTdp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 553.0506596652996,
      "y": 642.2195292756121,
      "width": 750.2395629882812,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b50",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1938300001,
      "version": 83,
      "versionNonce": 1922719727,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785931966755,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. keep looping while any of these is true: i >= 0, or j >= 0, or carry is not 0.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5. keep looping while any of these is true: i >= 0, or j >= 0, or carry is not 0.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aBHwoZIPW84hn1q3d_NGf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 550.4173867387027,
      "y": 674.6850612068158,
      "width": 1325.5390625,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b51",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1652688719,
      "version": 80,
      "versionNonce": 1655642753,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785931966755,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. (Three conditions, joined by OR. The carry one is what appends that final extra digit — like the leading 1 in 100.)\n6. Each pass, start sum at carry.\n7. If i >= 0: add digit at a[i] to sum, then move i one step left.\nIf i < 0: add nothing — a ran out, missing digits are 0.\n8. Same for j and b.\n9. Digit to write = sum % 2.\n10. New carry = Math.floor(sum / 2).\n11. Attach the written digit to result — on the left side, since you're producing digits right-to-left but the answer reads left-to-right.\n\nFinish\n\n12. Return result.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5. (Three conditions, joined by OR. The carry one is what appends that final extra digit — like the leading 1 in 100.)\n6. Each pass, start sum at carry.\n7. If i >= 0: add digit at a[i] to sum, then move i one step left.\nIf i < 0: add nothing — a ran out, missing digits are 0.\n8. Same for j and b.\n9. Digit to write = sum % 2.\n10. New carry = Math.floor(sum / 2).\n11. Attach the written digit to result — on the left side, since you're producing digits right-to-left but the answer reads left-to-right.\n\nFinish\n\n12. Return result.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "EwUHdjU18rEZlRXRKCsOP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 484.08347527447756,
      "y": 519.872629698756,
      "width": 1143.1192626953125,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b52",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 768221793,
      "version": 274,
      "versionNonce": 651963073,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785933637955,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Setup\n\n1. Pointer i = index of last character of a (that's a.length - 1).\n2. Pointer j = index of last character of b.\n3. carry = 0.\n4. result = empty string.\n\nLoop\n\n5. Keep looping while any of these is true: i >= 0, or j >= 0, or carry is not 0.\n\n5. (Three conditions, joined by OR. The carry one is what appends that final extra digit — like the leading 1 in 100.)\n6. Each pass, start sum at carry.\n7. If i >= 0: add digit at a[i] to sum, then move i one step left.\nIf i < 0: add nothing — a ran out, missing digits are 0.\n8. Same for j and b.\n9. Digit to write = sum % 2.\n10. New carry = Math.floor(sum / 2).\n11. Attach the written digit to result — on the left side, since \nyou're producing digits right-to-left but the answer reads left-to-right.\n\nFinish\n\n12. Return result.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Setup\n\n1. Pointer i = index of last character of a (that's a.length - 1).\n2. Pointer j = index of last character of b.\n3. carry = 0.\n4. result = empty string.\n\nLoop\n\n5. Keep looping while any of these is true: i >= 0, or j >= 0, or carry is not 0.\n\n5. (Three conditions, joined by OR. The carry one is what appends that final extra digit — like the leading 1 in 100.)\n6. Each pass, start sum at carry.\n7. If i >= 0: add digit at a[i] to sum, then move i one step left.\nIf i < 0: add nothing — a ran out, missing digits are 0.\n8. Same for j and b.\n9. Digit to write = sum % 2.\n10. New carry = Math.floor(sum / 2).\n11. Attach the written digit to result — on the left side, since \nyou're producing digits right-to-left but the answer reads left-to-right.\n\nFinish\n\n12. Return result.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
